cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this release, please cite Resolutive Science v0.4.0."
title: "Resolutive Science: Post-Falsification Diagnostic Release"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-09-08"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Matos"
    given-names: "Marcelo Roldão"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6075-4680"
repository-code: "https://github.com/marceloroldao/resolutive-science"
url: "https://github.com/marceloroldao/resolutive-science"
abstract: >-
  Resolutive Science v0.4.0 is a post-falsification diagnostic release for the
  frozen one-parameter RCMS cosmological screening surrogate. It adds Protocols
  17–20, testing residual topology, radial/transverse parameter consistency,
  redshift locality with look-elsewhere calibration, and exact-redshift
  cross-survey concordance between DESI DR2 and BOSS DR12. The diagnostic block
  finds diffuse post-fit residual structure, a DESI-specific channel tension,
  no calibrated redshift-locality evidence, and an exact-z survey discordance
  at z=0.51. The preregistered development stop gate is therefore activated as
  DIAGNOSTIC_STOP_NO_EXTENSION: no new cosmological RCMS functional form is
  generated from the same residuals. This release does not claim discovery of
  new physics or experimental validation of Resolutive Physics.
keywords:
